                        


Item #:  SCP-5215

Object Class:  Keter

Special Containment Procedures:  A perimeter has been established around SCP-5215 with an electric fence charged up to 300.000 volts, a metal gate at about 5 meters height using a magnetic seal lock, and sniper towers at every edge of the perimeter. Also at least 2 surveillance MQ-9 Reaper predator drones are to be present at the general air space of the containment site at all times. Should the site experience a power failure, on-site personnel are to utilize backup generators to reestablish communication with the active Security Chief as soon as possible. During an SCP-5215-2 instance, breach said instance is to be shot by one of the sniper towers which are equipped with anti-material rifles loaded with .308 Lapua rounds to terminate the subject. If the subject survives the shots, one of the on-site GCSs(Ground Control Stations) is to use predator drones to launch at least two AGM-114 Hellfire missiles. If more than 5 SCP-5215-2 instances reach the gate Mobile Task Force unit Nu-7 designated  is to be dispatched with one goal which is to terminate the SCP-5215-2 instances as soon as possible because their extremely unpredictable behavior can cause damage to neighboring areas as well as a breach of secrecy to the foundation, with the one exception of SCP-5215-1(see addendum 5215-A for details).

Description:  SCP-5215 is a remote village named  are the following: World war 1 and 2, the Vietnam war, the cold war, the Afghanistan invasion, Iraq, etc. These anomalous events only occur under circumstances that are not yet known. The SCP-5215 population is around 70 people which are to be labeled SCP5215-2. Said subjects usually pass the age of 60 but all of them show advanced metabolism, motor skills, and huge life spans reaching up to 300000. Three of these inhabitants however retain abilities that can potentially cause a lot of damage should a total containment failure occur, therefore they are to be labeled SCP-5215-1 instances (check addendum 5215-A B and C). However, these SCP-5215-1 instances show to be more advanced at everything and potentially be immortal. Said instance is extremely hard to contain due to it being extremely resistant to most forms of physical damage, very intelligent, and immune to the effects of every other SCP.

Addendum:  Addendum: SCP-5215-A: SCP-5215-1-A is a humanoid male that goes by the name of  which slows him down and damages him enough forcing him to enter a dormant state for about 15 minutes. Because of the nature of SCP-5215-1-A containment breaches happen once or twice a month. Due to the immense amount of resources needed to re-contain SCP-5215-1-A, a termination request has been sent to the O5 council and is still awaiting confirmation.

Addendum:  SCP-5215-1-B: SCP-5215-1-B is a humanoid male that goes by the name of .SCP-5215-1-A has control over every road in the SCP-5215. Other than this information not much is known about SCP-5215-1-B due to its anonymous nature.

Addendum:  SCP-5215-1-C: SCP-5215-1-C is a humanoid male that is named  according to the SCP-5215-2 instances that are not hostile.

Testing Logs: 

Test Log SCP-5215-Alpha: at ██/██/████, two D class personnel, D-2459, and D-3951, are given radios and navigators and are instructed to move closer to the village. At about 140 meters from the village, D-2459 reports a strange mist 40 meters from his position, though D-3951 reported nothing. D-2459 is ordered to proceed to the mist. When he reached the mist radio contact with D-2459 had been lost, therefore D-3951 was told to go search for D-2459. After 30 minutes D-3951 found D-2459 who had forgotten why he was there and was in a distressed state not being able to think straight. The test was called to a close and the class d personnel were called back due to lack of researchable material.

Results: New ability has been discovered.

Assessment: Further research is required.

Test Log SCP-5215-Beta:  D-8392 is sent 150 meters away from the entrance and is told to describe what he sees over the radio.




