D-8392 is sent 100 meters away from the entrance and is told to keep walking no matter what. He is given a note that says . D-6721 is sent 150 meters away from the entrance and is told to observe D-8392.

D-6721 reports seeing D-8392 collapse and stay like that for 25 minutes. After said time subject is reported to wake up, extremely distressed. Radio communication with D-8392 is lost. The subject takes a note out of his pocket, reads it, and proceeds to use a pen that was put in his pocket to take notes after 3 minutes subject starts walking around and is no longer able to be seen by D-6721, who reports she only sees fog after a certain distance. Subject D-8392 after 20 minutes returns to D-6721. Both subjects return to the researcher team.

D-8392's note:  

Test Log SCP-5215-Charlie: Two Class-D personnel, D-7193, and D-9185 are instructed to enter SCP-5215 and attempt to make contact with SCP-5215-1-A to learn something new about it. One hour in both D-7193 and D-9185 report that they saw a strange humanoid entity roaming the streets of SCP-5215 so they are instructed by the researcher team to approach it. Upon closer inspection, the entity was SCP-5215-1-A, and immediately after reaching it, the entity released a liquid acid-like substance on both D class personnel. Shortly after both of them were dead. Thirty seconds later SCP-5215-1-B appeared out of an abandoned house and started shaping roads for the substance to flow downhill towards the researchers. Minutes later SCP-5215-1-A and B alongside 50 SCP-5215-2 instances attempted to breach containment using the acid as cover for their advance. Mobile Task Force unit Nu-7 designated Maz Hatters to clear the acid so MTF could proceed with the elimination of all SCP-5215-2 instances and attempt to re contain SCP-5215-1-A and B. One hour later all SCP-5215-2 instances were eliminated and SCP-5215-1-A and B retreated to SCP-5215.

Results: More than 10 MTF soldiers were eliminated 34 were injured and two helicopters were bought down by SCP-5215-A. Though samples of the acid were collected by Mobile Task Force unit Beta-7 and research is undergoing.



                    

                                    





            
    

                    



                    
                        
                            
